# Scoped licenses for version 1.1.0 reproducibility materials

Copyright 2026 Yunya Lin.

The exact per-file assignments are in `manifests/license_scope.csv`: MIT for named original Python research/reporting/test code; CC BY 4.0 for named original derived non-text outputs, identifier projections, configurations, provenance and documentation. The candidate's new grants become operative only after the author's explicit approval for publication of this exact scope. Earlier approved grants for unchanged historical files remain intact. No blanket grant applies to arbitrary future files.

CC BY 4.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ ; legal code: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode.en . Attribute Yunya Lin, retain notices and indicate modifications. Grants apply only to rights the author is authorized to license; they create no rights over facts or public-domain elements.

Excluded: full source titles/abstracts/author lists, raw provider text, embeddings, model weights, complete masked scalar and focal-neighbor records, external libraries/templates/fonts, licensed literature, private project history/audits, and the manuscript/source. Referencing a dependency, identifier, model revision or hash does not relicense that material. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and docs/license_scope_policy.md.

